{
  "_note": "Per-ZIP cost of living for ARKANSAS and every county bordering it. The base model in peer-benchmarks.json is 3-digit prefix -> one of four tiers, and all fourteen Arkansas prefixes (716-729) were already in it \u2014 but Little Rock, Fayetteville, Springdale and Bentonville all landed on 'moderate', which is exactly 1.0 across all twelve categories, so the onboarding chart drew two identical bars and Arkansas looked absent. It was not absent; it was flat. This file resolves a ZIP to its own COUNTY instead. Sources: ZIP -> county from the public us-state-county-zip dataset (scpike, US Census-derived); county home values from Zillow's public county-level ZHVI CSV, month 2026-07-31. Prototype-grade (D19) \u2014 editable, not a live feed, not advice.",
  "method": {
    "_note": "A county's ratio is its typical home value over the national median county home value. That ratio is placed on the SAME four-tier ladder peer-benchmarks.json already defines, and the twelve category multipliers are interpolated linearly between the two bracketing tiers (benchInterpolateTiers, js/benchmarks.js), clamping outside them. Nothing here invents a new category shape \u2014 a county lands somewhere on the existing low <-> very_high continuum instead of being rounded to one of four rungs.",
    "nationalMedianCountyHomeValue": 234352,
    "tierAnchors": {
      "low": 0.55,
      "moderate": 1.0,
      "high": 1.6,
      "very_high": 2.6
    },
    "estimatedCounties": [
      "AR:Nevada"
    ],
    "_estimatedNote": "No ZHVI coverage, so these fall back to the Arkansas county median (166,302). Flagged rather than silently averaged."
  },
